Z||000005||Kelvin Vivian||04-10-2001||02:51 AM||||That's a pretty 85 GT, it's a manual Fiero too!<P>Songman,<P>I believe that all 85 V6s, GTs and SEs, did not have the extra gauge pod in the center... <P>All 1987 and 1988 Fiero V6s had the auxiliary pods... And in 1986, some V6s received them and others did not. I do not know when the auxiliary center pods were added in 86... perhaps at the same time the 5-spd Getrags became available, maybe b4 then. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||AusFiero||04-10-2001||06:35 AM||||The Fiero auxillary gauges were available in 86 models from at least July 86. My July 86 GT Fastback has them...and they are factory.<BR>How long before that...who knows.||||reg||1
